    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; `AcceptanceBase` is an abstract helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner representation to expose `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner's id. The codebase generates `OwnerDto` from `openapi.yml` and populates read-only computed fields (like `locality`, `customerCode`, `telephoneDisplay`) via matching getters on the `Owner` entity, mapped by name through MapStruct. I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `selfLink` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getSelfLink()` getter returning `\"/api/owners/\" + getId()` (null-guarded for an owner with no id yet). MapStruct maps it by name into the DTO, so it's returned from both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsSelfLink` \u2014 which creates a structured owner and asserts `$.selfLink` equals `/api/owners/{id}` on the GET \u2014 now passes.",
